  "bull_bear_summary": {
    "bull_case": "Niccol turnaround gaining traction (first positive U.S. traffic in 8 quarters, +3% transaction growth Q1 FY2026). Powerful brand with 30.9% U.S. market share (2.7x Dunkin). Massive store growth runway to 55K by 2030. Menu innovation (Cold Foam = $1B+ customization biz). China JV with Boyu Capital to go asset-light. FY2028 EPS target $3.35-$4.00 implies significant margin recovery. Bull valuation ~$120/share assumes P/E >36x and stronger margins.",
    "bear_case": "Forward P/E ~40x prices in perfect execution of turnaround still in early innings. Operating margins compressed in Q1 FY2026 despite revenue beat — turnaround costs front-loaded. FY2026 EPS guidance $2.15-$2.40 implies only modest improvement. China comp sales were -8% in FY2024, intense Luckin Coffee competition. Coffee/tariff cost headwinds squeezing margins. Dutch Bros and 7 Brew fragmenting U.S. market. DCF-based bear valuation ~$67-$73/share (Simply Wall St). Stagnant margin expansion over the last decade (FY2013 16.5% vs FY2023 16.3%).",
    "dm": {"type": "S", "source": "Motley Fool, Simply Wall St, CNBC, Axios, TheStreet", "note": "Synthesized from multiple analyst/media sources. Bull/bear framing is editorial synthesis, not a single analyst's view."}
  },
